% Daml patterns: locking a coin by changing its state
%
% The Logical English (for LPS) twin of a Daml project, written by the Daml translator
% from its source: each template a fluent keyed by the contract id, each create and choice an action,
% who may do what integrity constraints. The source is kept in sources/ (File > Show the Original in the
% Logical English editor, View > The original this was converted from in the LPS2 IDE).
% The ids of the contracts a command creates are places of its action: the ledger assigns them, a scenario names them.
% Who may do what, as one permission per command: the legal view
% (Misc > Legal View of This LPS Program in the Logical English editor, View > Legal view in the LPS2 IDE).

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 9.

the actions are:
    *a party* creates the lockable coin *a lockable coin* with owner *an owner*, issuer *an issuer*, amount *an amount* and locker *a locker*; known as create_lockable_coin.
    *a party* creates the transfer proposal *a transfer proposal* with coin owner *a coin owner*, coin issuer *a coin issuer*, coin amount *a coin amount*, coin locker *a coin locker* and new owner *a new owner*; known as create_transfer_proposal.
    *a party* creates the coin proposal *a coin proposal* with owner *an owner*, issuer *an issuer* and amount *an amount*; known as create_coin_proposal.
    *a party* archives the lockable coin *a lockable coin*; known as archive_lockable_coin.
    *a party* archives the transfer proposal *a transfer proposal*; known as archive_transfer_proposal.
    *a party* archives the coin proposal *a coin proposal*; known as archive_coin_proposal.
    *a party* exercises transfer on the lockable coin *a lockable coin* with new owner *a new owner* creating *a transfer proposal*; known as transfer.
    *a party* exercises lock on the lockable coin *a lockable coin* with new locker *a new locker* creating *a second lockable coin*; known as lock.
    *a party* exercises unlock on the lockable coin *a lockable coin* creating *a second lockable coin*; known as unlock.
    *a party* exercises withdraw transfer on the transfer proposal *a transfer proposal* creating *a lockable coin*; known as withdraw_transfer.
    *a party* exercises accept transfer on the transfer proposal *a transfer proposal* creating *a lockable coin*; known as accept_transfer.
    *a party* exercises reject transfer on the transfer proposal *a transfer proposal*; known as reject_transfer.
    *a party* exercises accept proposal on the coin proposal *a coin proposal* creating *a lockable coin*; known as accept_proposal.

the fluents are:
    *a lockable coin* is a lockable coin with owner *an owner*, issuer *an issuer*, amount *an amount* and locker *a locker*; known as lockable_coin.
    *a transfer proposal* is a transfer proposal with coin owner *a coin owner*, coin issuer *a coin issuer*, coin amount *a coin amount*, coin locker *a coin locker* and new owner *a new owner*; known as transfer_proposal.
    *a coin proposal* is a coin proposal with owner *an owner*, issuer *an issuer* and amount *an amount*; known as coin_proposal.

the knowledge base locking includes:

the text of "the source daml/LockingByChangingState.daml" is at "sources/daml/LockingByChangingState.daml".

the text of "the source daml/Utilities.daml" is at "sources/daml/Utilities.daml".

% LockableCoin: a party creates one; its signatories must be the one who submits (Daml's authorization)
when a party creates the lockable coin a lockable coin with owner an owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
then the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner the owner, issuer the issuer, amount the amount and locker the locker.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the lockable coin a lockable coin with owner an owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
    and the party is different from the issuer.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the lockable coin a lockable coin with owner an owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
    and the party is different from the owner.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the lockable coin a lockable coin with owner an owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
    and the amount <= 0.0.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the lockable coin a lockable coin with owner an owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
    and the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner a second owner, issuer a second issuer, amount a second amount and locker a second locker.

% LockableCoin: archiving one (Daml's Archive choice) is for its signatories, and it must be active
when a party archives the lockable coin a lockable coin
    and the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner an owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
then it is not the case that the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner the owner, issuer the issuer, amount the amount and locker the locker.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the lockable coin a lockable coin
    and the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner an owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
    and the party is different from the issuer.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the lockable coin a lockable coin
    and the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner an owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
    and the party is different from the owner.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the lockable coin a lockable coin
    and it is not the case that the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner an owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker.

% LockableCoin.Transfer (consuming): the controller (owner) must submit it, and the contract must be active
when a party exercises transfer on the lockable coin a lockable coin with new owner an owner creating a transfer proposal
    and the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner a second owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
then the transfer proposal is a transfer proposal with coin owner the second owner, coin issuer the issuer, coin amount the amount, coin locker the locker and new owner the owner
    and it is not the case that the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner the second owner, issuer the issuer, amount the amount and locker the locker.

it must not be true that
    a party exercises transfer on the lockable coin a lockable coin with new owner an owner creating a transfer proposal
    and the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner a second owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
    and the party is different from the second owner.

it must not be true that
    a party exercises transfer on the lockable coin a lockable coin with new owner an owner creating a transfer proposal
    and it is not the case that the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner a second owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker.

it must not be true that
    a party exercises transfer on the lockable coin a lockable coin with new owner an owner creating a transfer proposal
    and the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner a second owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a locker
    and the locker is different from the second owner.

% LockableCoin.Lock (consuming): the controller (owner) must submit it, and the contract must be active
when a party exercises lock on the lockable coin a lockable coin with new locker a locker creating a second lockable coin
    and the lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner an owner, issuer an issuer, amount an amount and locker a second locker
then the second lockable coin is a lockable coin with owner the owner, issuer the issuer, amount the amount and locker the locker
