% Daml (the script run on a Canton sandbox) ends with these active contracts (their payloads;
% the ids are the ledger's):
%   - lockable_coin(you,bank,100.0,you)
% The twin's final state under LPS2 (`lps state`) is compared with it by test_daml.pl.
scenario locking is:
    % the Daml Script locking
    bank creates the coin proposal prop_id with owner me, issuer bank and amount 100.0 from 1 to 2.
    me exercises accept proposal on the coin proposal prop_id creating coin_cid from 2 to 3.
    me exercises lock on the lockable coin coin_cid with new locker custodian bank creating locked_cid from 3 to 4.
    % Daml refuses the next command (submitMustFail): the twin's integrity constraints refuse it
    me exercises transfer on the lockable coin locked_cid with new owner you creating c1 from 4 to 5.
    custodian bank exercises unlock on the lockable coin locked_cid creating unlocked_cid from 5 to 6.
    me exercises transfer on the lockable coin unlocked_cid with new owner you creating prop_id from 6 to 7.
    you exercises accept transfer on the transfer proposal prop_id creating c2 from 7 to 8.

